## a b s t r a c t
Developing low-cost non-precious metals as efficient catalysts for the reduction of toxic 4-nitrophenol (4-NP) to useful 4-aminophenol (4-AP) have received increasing attention in recent years. Herein, a novel and efficient Cu-based catalyst $\mathsf{C u}/\mathsf{C u}_{\mathsf{x}}\mathsf{O@C N}$ (carbon doped with nitrogen) was prepared via a facile method from pyrolysis of bi-ligand MOFs material $\mathsf{C u}_{2}(\mathsf{B D C})_{2}(\mathsf{B P Y})$ $({\mathsf{B D C}}={\mathsf{p}}$ -Phthalic acid, $\mathsf{B P Y}=4,4^{\prime}{-}\mathsf{b}$ ipyridyl) in Ar atmosphere. Characterization results revealed that N doping in carbon matrix favors the development of mesoporous structure, the formation of more defect sites in carbon matrix, better dispersion of $\mathtt{C u}/\mathtt{C u}_{\mathrm{x}}0$ nano particles, and maintenance of Cu species in metallic Cu state (the active site), all of which contribute to a superior catalytic activity for 4-NP reduction with a pseudo-first-order rate constant as high as $0.126s^{-1}$ (the molar ratio of $\mathsf{N a B H}_{4}$ to 4-NP is 400), nearly 11 times higher than its counterpart $\mathsf{C u}/\mathsf{C u}_{\mathrm{x}}\mathsf{O@C}$ without N doping $(0.011\ s^{-1}\cdot$ . The activation energy for 4-NP reduction to 4-AP catalyzed by $\mathtt{C u}/\mathtt{C u}_{\mathrm{x}}0@\mathtt{C N}$ was determined as $55.6~\mathrm{kJ~mol}^{-1}$ (the molar ratio of $\mathsf{N a B H}_{4}$ to 4-NP is 100). In addition, $\mathsf{C u}/\mathsf{C u}_{\mathrm{x}}\mathsf{O@C N}$ showed excellent reusability in successive 6 cycles. The facile synthesis and superior catalytic activity make $\mathsf{C u}/\mathsf{C u}_{\mathsf{x}}\mathsf{O@C N}$ a promising catalyst in industrial applications for many other similar reaction systems.
